# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AEGIS environment template. Copy to `.env` and edit. `.env` is git-ignored.
# These are the environment variables actually read by the code today
# (`src/aegis/api/settings.py`, `web/src/api/config.ts`). Nothing else in the
# repo reads an environment variable -- training/generation scripts take
# every path and seed as an explicit CLI argument instead (see `--help` on
# any script under `scripts/`, or docs/DEPLOYMENT.md).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Backend (aegis.api, FastAPI) -------------------------------------------

# Repository root the API reads `models/` and `data/` under. Defaults to the
# real repo root when unset -- only set this to point the API at a different
# artifacts tree (e.g. a curated deployment bundle; see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md).
# AEGIS_ARTIFACTS_ROOT=/path/to/artifacts
#
# Clean clone / no local pipeline run yet: this repo tracks a minimal, real
# demo-artifact bundle at submission/artifacts/ (see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md
# "Clean-clone quick start") that needs no PaySim download or training step.
# AEGIS_ARTIFACTS_ROOT=submission/artifacts

# Comma-separated list of origins the API's CORS middleware allows. Defaults
# to the Vite dev server (http://localhost:5173, http://127.0.0.1:5173) when
# unset. Set this to your deployed frontend's origin in production.
# AEGIS_API_CORS_ORIGINS=https://your-frontend.example.com

# --- Frontend (web/, Vite) ---------------------------------------------------

# Must be committed to web/.env (or set at build time), not this file --
# Vite only inlines variables prefixed VITE_ from its own working directory.
# Base URL of the deployed API. Left empty (the default), the frontend calls
# relative /api/... paths, which the Vite dev server proxies to
# http://localhost:8000 (see web/vite.config.ts) and which a static host must
# be configured to reverse-proxy to the API in production.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-api.example.com
